Subject: [PATCH] feat(plans): duration is the product, tier is an
 implementation detail (v1.9.1)

The owner sells 1, 3, 6 and 12 months of the same membership. He does not want
bronze, silver and diamond as products, and the app was printing the tier name
on the member's own card.

- GET /memberships/plans now returns durationDays (the raw integer) so a client
  can compute a per-month price without parsing "90_days".
- The plan form no longer offers a tier dropdown. The column stays and the
  current value is carried in a hidden input, because tier_rank() still gates
  course access and the upgrade path compares ranks; removing it from the
  schema would silently break entitlements. New plans default to bronze, so all
  four durations sit on one level.

No schema change, no migration: four duration plans are four rows the owner
already knows how to create.

Plugin 1.9.1. Tests: 324 pass.
